  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 930 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nOn Friday, the ridge to our west will expand and provide an \nincrease in heat concerns that will persist through the weekend. \nOtherwise, there's a low to medium chances (20-40%) for diurnal \nshowers and thunderstorms with the greatest coverage east of I-65.\nThis weekend, moisture will wrap around the western side of the \nsubtropical ridge out in the Atlantic and bring an increase in \nrainfall, low to medium (30-60%) chances Saturday through Monday. \nHighest coverage will again be east of I-65. Highs will be in the \nupper 80s to lower 90s Friday through Monday but heat index values\nwill push above 100 degrees. At this time, values remain just \nbelow Heat Advisory criteria however trends will be monitored. \nRegardless, practice heat safety!",
